# Views and Templates Guide

## View Files

Views are stored in module directories at [Body/{role}/{module}/Views/](mdc:Body) with `.ct` extension.

## Loading Views

### Using Loader
```php
// Single view
$this->load->view('public/Blog/index', $data);

// Multiple views (common pattern)
$this->load->view('public/Common/header', $data);
$this->load->view('public/Blog/index', $data);
$this->load->view('public/Common/footer', $data);
```

### View Path Format
```
"{role}/{module}/{viewname}"

Examples:
- "public/Home/home"
- "admin/Dashboard/index"
- "public/Common/header"
```

## Data Passing

### Controller to View
```php
public function index(): void
{
    $data = [
        'title' => 'Page Title',
        'items' => $this->model->getAll(),
        'user' => $this->session->get('user')
    ];
    
    $this->load->view('public/Module/index', $data);
}
```

### Accessing in View
```php
<h1><?= htmlspecialchars($title ?? 'Default Title') ?></h1>

<?php if (!empty($items)): ?>
    <?php foreach ($items as $item): ?>
        <p><?= htmlspecialchars($item['name']) ?></p>
    <?php endforeach; ?>
<?php endif; ?>
```

## Common Views

### Header ([Body/public/Common/Views/header.ct](mdc:Body/public/Common/Views/header.ct))
```php
<header id="header">
    <nav>
        <a href="<?= Router::url('home') ?>">Home</a>
        <a href="<?= Router::url('about') ?>">About</a>
    </nav>
</header>

<?php renderBreadcrumb(); ?>
```

### Footer ([Body/public/Common/Views/footer.ct](mdc:Body/public/Common/Views/footer.ct))
```php
<footer style="padding:16px;background:#333;color:#fff;">
    <p>&copy; <?= date('Y') ?> CyberTirah Framework</p>
</footer>
```

## Breadcrumb System

### Automatic Breadcrumbs
Breadcrumbs are automatically generated from the URL path.

```php
// In header.ct
renderBreadcrumb(); // Generates from current URL
```

### Custom Breadcrumbs
```php
$customBreadcrumbs = [
    ['label' => 'Home', 'url' => '/'],
    ['label' => 'Products', 'url' => '/products'],
    ['label' => 'Electronics', 'url' => '/products/electronics'],
    ['label' => 'Item Name', 'url' => '']
];

renderBreadcrumb($customBreadcrumbs);
```

### Breadcrumb Dictionary
Add custom term mappings in header.ct:

```php
function getBreadcrumbDictionary()
{
    return [
        "index" => "Home",
        "about" => "About Us",
        "team" => "Our Team",
        // Add custom mappings
        "blog" => "Our Blog",
        "products" => "Products",
    ];
}
```

## URL Generation in Views

### Named Routes
```php
<a href="<?= Router::url('blog.show', ['id' => $post['id']]) ?>">
    Read More
</a>

<a href="<?= Router::url('blog.index', [], ['page' => 2]) ?>">
    Page 2
</a>
```

### Direct URLs
```php
<a href="/about">About Us</a>
<a href="/about/team">Our Team</a>
```

## HTML Output Escaping

### Always Escape User Data
```php
<!-- Good -->
<h1><?= htmlspecialchars($title) ?></h1>
<p><?= htmlspecialchars($content) ?></p>

<!-- Bad (XSS vulnerability) -->
<h1><?= $title ?></h1>
<p><?= $content ?></p>
```

### Safe HTML Output
```php
<!-- For trusted HTML content -->
<?= $trustedHtml ?>

<!-- For user content, use purifier -->
<?= $htmlPurifier->purify($userContent) ?>
```

## Conditional Rendering

### Check Data Existence
```php
<?php if (!empty($items)): ?>
    <!-- Render items -->
<?php else: ?>
    <p>No items found.</p>
<?php endif; ?>
```

### User Authentication
```php
<?php if ($this->session->has('user_id')): ?>
    <a href="/logout">Logout</a>
<?php else: ?>
    <a href="/login">Login</a>
<?php endif; ?>
```

## Styling Patterns

### Inline Styles (Current Pattern)
```php
<div style="max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:20px;">
    <h1 style="color:#667eea;font-size:2em;">Title</h1>
</div>
```

### CSS Classes (Alternative)
```php
<div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Title</h1>
</div>
```

## Common View Patterns

### List View
```php
<div class="items-list">
    <?php if (!empty($items)): ?>
        <?php foreach ($items as $item): ?>
            <div class="item-card">
                <h3><?= htmlspecialchars($item['title']) ?></h3>
                <p><?= htmlspecialchars($item['description']) ?></p>
                <a href="<?= Router::url('item.show', ['id' => $item['id']]) ?>">
                    View Details
                </a>
            </div>
        <?php endforeach; ?>
    <?php else: ?>
        <p>No items to display.</p>
    <?php endif; ?>
</div>
```

### Detail View
```php
<div class="item-detail">
    <h1><?= htmlspecialchars($item['title']) ?></h1>
    
    <div class="metadata">
        <span>Created: <?= date('F j, Y', strtotime($item['created_at'])) ?></span>
        <span>Author: <?= htmlspecialchars($item['author']) ?></span>
    </div>
    
    <div class="content">
        <?= nl2br(htmlspecialchars($item['content'])) ?>
    </div>
    
    <a href="<?= Router::url('items.index') ?>">Back to List</a>
</div>
```

### Form View
```php
<form method="POST" action="<?= Router::url('item.store') ?>">
    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Title</label>
        <input type="text" name="title" required 
               value="<?= htmlspecialchars($item['title'] ?? '') ?>">
    </div>
    
    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Content</label>
        <textarea name="content" required><?= htmlspecialchars($item['content'] ?? '') ?></textarea>
    </div>
    
    <button type="submit">Save</button>
</form>
```

## Best Practices

1. **Always escape output**: Use `htmlspecialchars()` for user data
2. **Use named routes**: For all URLs to enable easy refactoring
3. **Check data existence**: Use `??` operator for defaults
4. **Separate concerns**: Keep logic in controllers, display in views
5. **Reuse common views**: header, footer, navigation
6. **Use breadcrumbs**: Call `renderBreadcrumb()` for navigation context
7. **Semantic HTML**: Use proper HTML5 elements
8. **Responsive design**: Consider mobile-first approach
9. **Accessibility**: Use proper ARIA labels and semantic markup
10. **Performance**: Minimize inline styles, consider CSS classes for production
